.DS_Store
.build/
build/
*.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/
DerivedData/

# The crew is local. Fourteen agent definitions and the plugin that installs
# them live on disk and are not part of the project's history: they are how one
# person drives this repository, not something it ships. `/plugin marketplace
# add ~/Projects/Claude/Helm` reads them from the working copy, so nothing about
# installing them needed git.
/.claude/agents/
/plugins/
/.claude-plugin/

# The reasoning stays private. ARCHITECTURE.md, CLAUDE.md and the docs/ tree of
# specs and plans are how this app is built rather than something it ships; they
# live on disk and in a private repository. The public tree carries the code,
# the changelog, the licence notice and how to build it.
# These three are symbolic links into `helm-backstage`, a private repository
# that holds everything about Helm that Helm does not ship. They were plain
# copies until 2026-08-03, kept in step by remembering to copy them — which
# meant they diverged: the backup sat a day behind and still described code the
# tree had rolled back, while looking like the source of truth.
#
# No trailing slash on `docs`. The pattern was `/docs/`, which matches a
# directory and not a link, so the moment the copy became a link it reappeared
# in `git status` — one character between "ignored" and "about to be committed
# into the public history".
/ARCHITECTURE.md
/CLAUDE.md
/docs

# Brainstorm sessions write HTML mockups here. They are working material for one
# design conversation — the decisions that survive them land in `docs/`, and the
# mockups themselves are worth keeping on disk and out of the history.
/.superpowers/
